{"A House Divided":"一个分裂的家庭","Hanzala ibn Abi Amir (RA) was a young man of the Aws in Madinah, and his household held one of the sharpest divides in the sirah. His father, Abu Amir, had been a religious figure of standing before Islam, and when the Prophet ﷺ arrived he refused the message, left the city in anger, and attached himself to Quraysh. The sirah writers record him at Uhud on the enemy side, calling on his old tribesmen to abandon their Prophet ﷺ, and being answered with curses by the very people he expected to follow him.":"罕兹莱·本·艾比·阿米尔（愿主喜悦他）是麦地那奥斯族的一个青年，他的家庭中有着《先知传》里最尖锐的分裂之一。他的父亲艾布·阿米尔在伊斯兰之前是一位颇有地位的宗教人物；先知ﷺ到来时，他拒绝了这一使命，愤然离开这座城市，投靠了古莱什人。传记作者们记载，他在吴侯德站在敌方一边，呼吁他昔日的族人抛弃他们的先知ﷺ，而他原以为会追随他的那些人却以诅咒回答了他。","The son took the opposite road with his whole heart. Hanzala believed, prayed, and grew up inside the first community of Madinah while his father campaigned against it, and the books give no report of the son ever wavering toward the father's side. Islam cut through households in that generation, and it asked of some believers a loyalty that ran against their own blood. What makes Hanzala's story endure is that this obedience, tested at home for years, was about to be tested in a single night.":"儿子则全心全意地走上了相反的道路。罕兹莱信道、礼拜，在麦地那的第一个穆斯林群体中成长，而他的父亲却在征战反对这个群体；典籍中没有任何记载说这个儿子曾经向父亲那一边动摇过。在那一代人中，伊斯兰穿透了一个个家庭，它要求一些信士献出一种与自己血缘相悖的忠诚。使罕兹莱的故事流传不衰的，是这种在家中经受了多年考验的服从，即将在一个夜晚里接受考验。","The Wedding Night":"新婚之夜","On the night before Uhud, Hanzala was married. The sirah writers relate that he asked the Prophet's ﷺ permission to remain that night in Madinah with his bride, and permission was given. The army prepared for battle while a young man began his married life inside the city, with leave from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ himself. Nothing in the arrangement was hidden or blameworthy; he was exactly where he had been permitted to be, doing what had been made lawful for him that very night.":"在吴侯德战役的前一夜，罕兹莱成婚了。传记作者们记述，他请求先知ﷺ允许他那一夜留在麦地那陪伴新娘，先知ﷺ准许了。大军在为战斗作准备，而一个青年却在城中开始了他的婚姻生活，得到的是真主的使者ﷺ本人的许可。这一安排中没有任何隐秘或可指摘之处；他恰恰在他被允许所在的地方，做着就在那一夜被定为合法的事。","At dawn came the call to arms, and Hanzala's answer is his whole measure. He rose and went straight out to the fighting without pausing for the ritual bath that the night obliged. The sirah writers keep the detail exactly as it is and add nothing to it: the call came, and he left. A man may love what is lawful and still leave it instantly when the summons of Allah and His Messenger ﷺ arrives. That morning walk from the bridal chamber to the battle line is his biography compressed.":"黎明时，出征的号召传来，而罕兹莱的回应就是他的全部分量。他起身径直奔赴战场，连那一夜使他必须进行的大净都没有停下来做。传记作者们原原本本地保留这个细节，丝毫不加添：号召来了，他就走了。一个人可以喜爱合法的事物，但当真主及其使者ﷺ的召唤到来时，仍能立刻舍下它。那天早晨从洞房走到战线的那段路，就是他浓缩的传记。","One Morning of War":"一个早晨的战争","Ibn Hisham traces his path through the field. Hanzala fought his way to Abu Sufyan, the commander of the Quraysh army, brought him down, and had the better of him, when Shaddad ibn al-Aswad struck Hanzala and killed him. He had been a bridegroom by night and was a martyr on the field by morning. The battle gave him no long career of campaigns to be remembered by; his fighting life lasted one morning, and it ended within reach of the enemy's own commander.":"伊本·希沙姆追溯了他在战场上的路线。罕兹莱一路杀到古莱什大军的统帅艾布·苏富扬跟前，把他打倒在地，占了上风，就在这时，舍达德·本·艾斯沃德砍中罕兹莱，杀死了他。他在夜里是新郎，到了早晨已是战场上的殉道者。这场战役没有给他留下一段可供人追忆的漫长征战生涯；他的战斗生命只持续了一个早晨，而它结束的地方，离敌军的统帅本人只有咫尺之遥。","No one on the field that morning knew what his death had just earned. To the eye he was one more of the believers cut down in the hour the ranks broke, a young man whose war had lasted from dawn to midmorning. The sirah writers record no dying speech from him. The honour that would attach itself to his name for all time was announced not by men at all, but from where the Prophet ﷺ alone could see.":"那天早晨，战场上没有人知道他的死刚刚赢得了什么。在人们眼里，他不过是阵线崩溃那一刻倒下的又一位信士，一个战争从黎明持续到上午的青年。传记作者们没有记载他的任何临终遗言。那份将永远附着于他名字之上的荣誉，根本不是由人宣布的，而是来自唯有先知ﷺ才能看见的地方。","Washed by the Angels":"天神为他洗身","After the battle the Prophet ﷺ told his companions that he had seen the angels washing Hanzala between the sky and the earth, and he directed them to ask his wife. She told them that he had gone out at the call in a state that required the ritual bath, with no time to perform it. That, the report concludes, is why the angels washed him. The account comes through the sirah writers and the later collections rather than the two Sahihs, and the ummah has received it from them generation after generation.":"战斗结束后，先知ﷺ告诉他的弟子们，他看见天神们在天地之间为罕兹莱洗身，并吩咐他们去问他的妻子。她告诉他们，他是在必须做大净的状态下应召出征的，没有时间去做。传述的结论说，这就是天神们为他洗身的原因。这一记载来自传记作者们和后来的圣训集，而不是两部《圣训实录》，稳麦一代又一代地从他们那里接受了它。","From that day he has been called Ghasil al-Mala'ikah, the one washed by the angels. Consider what the title certifies. The bath he missed was not neglect but obedience; he set aside even a lawful joy and a duty's appointed washing because the summons to fight had arrived. Allah answered the unfinished purification with a purification no living man receives. The believer's smallest circumstances are seen and weighed, and nothing sincere goes missing. That is the teaching the ummah reads out of one dawn in one household.":"从那一天起，他就被称为“盖西勒·麦拉伊凯”，即天神为之洗身的人。想一想这个称号所证明的是什么。他错过的那次沐浴不是疏忽，而是服从；因为出征的召唤已经到来，他连一份合法的欢乐和一项义务规定的洗浴都放下了。真主以一种没有任何活人能够得到的洁净，回应了那未完成的洁净。信士最微小的境况都被看见、被衡量，凡是真诚的，没有一样会遗失。这就是稳麦从一个家庭的一个黎明中读出的教诲。","The Name That Remained":"留存下来的名号","The title outlived him in his own line. The historians relate that his son Abdullah ibn Hanzala, born of the bride of that single night, was known in Madinah all his life as the son of the one washed by the angels, and grew into a man of standing among the next generation. A marriage of one night, ended by martyrdom, still planted a household in Islam. The father who had fought against the Prophet ﷺ, the historians add, died far from Madinah, alone in his refusal.":"这个称号在他自己的后代中比他活得更久。史学家们记述，他的儿子阿卜杜拉·本·罕兹莱——由那唯一一夜的新娘所生——一生在麦地那都被称为“天神为之洗身者的儿子”，并成长为下一代人中一位有地位的人物。一场只有一夜、以殉道告终的婚姻，仍然在伊斯兰中扎下了一个家庭。史学家们还补充说，那位曾与先知ﷺ为敌的父亲，死在远离麦地那的地方，在他的拒绝中孤独地死去。","Hanzala's story is told wherever the sirah is taught, because it needs no embellishment to do its work. A believer's ordinary night and extraordinary morning sit side by side, and heaven's response to both is on record. The scholars warn against adding details the sources do not give, for the account as the sirah writers left it is already complete: the call of Allah outweighed every pull of the world, and the angels themselves confirmed the exchange in the sight of the Prophet ﷺ.":"凡是讲授《先知传》的地方，都会讲到罕兹莱的故事，因为它无需任何渲染就能发挥作用。一位信士平凡的夜晚与非凡的早晨并列在一起，而上天对两者的回应都有据可查。学者们告诫人们不要添加史料没有提供的细节，因为传记作者们所留下的记载本身已经完整：真主的召唤压倒了尘世的一切牵引，而天神们亲自在先知ﷺ的眼前证实了这场交换。"}